  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new test binary, `crates/post/tests/ream_lathe.rs`, posts an axial ream on the spindle centreline through each shipped lathe post.\n- `fanuc-lathe` posts on `assets/machines/lathe.mch`. `tormach-lathe` posts on `assets/machines/tormach-15l-slant-pro.mch`.\n- Two new goldens: `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/fanuc-lathe.nc` and `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/tormach-lathe.nc`.\n- A decision file: `docs/decisions/1481-ream-lathe-posts.md`.\n- No post script changed. No source file changed.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe ream slice of #1445 mapped REAM to `G85` in `fanuc-lathe.cps`. No test posted a ream through a lathe post. The two lathe posts already post the ream correctly on `upstream/main`. This PR adds the pins that the issue asks for.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll tests are in `camcraft-post`, binary `ream_lathe`.\n\n- `every_lathe_post_is_covered`: each `*lathe*.cps` post has a row in the test.\n- `the_stream_names_the_axial_ream`: the stream carries `CYCLE REAM` on X 0 Y 0.\n- `fanuc_lathe_posts_g85_and_no_other_cycle`: one `G85`, no other cycle word, no `P` or `Q` word. The tool is on R on the centreline before `G85`. `G80` comes before the exit rapid. No chain move doubles the cycle.\n- `tormach_lathe_feeds_in_and_feeds_out_of_the_reamed_hole`: no canned cycle word. The tool feeds in and feeds out at the same F. The retract is not a rapid.\n- `a_ream_with_a_dwell_keeps_its_cycle_on_both_posts`: `G85 P500` on `fanuc-lathe`, `G4 P0.5` at the floor on `tormach-lathe`.\n- `a_ream_off_the_spindle_axis_is_refused_by_name`: the two posts give the warning \"drilling cycle off the spindle axis\" and write no cycle word.\n- `the_lathe_posts_post_the_ream_byte_exact`: the two goldens.\n\nRed before the change: only `the_lathe_posts_post_the_ream_byte_exact` was red on unchanged code, because the golden files did not exist. The behaviour tests were green on unchanged code. The work that the issue owes is the tests and the goldens.\n\nMutations of the post scripts (each one restored after the run):\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `fanuc-lathe.cps`: remove the `REAM` to `G85` line (the ream falls to `G83`) | red: `fanuc_lathe_posts_g85_and_no_other_cycle`, the dwell test, the golden test |\n| `tormach-lathe.cps`: refuse `REAM` as it refuses `TAP` | red: `tormach_lathe_feeds_in_and_feeds_out_of_the_reamed_hole`, the dwell test, the golden test |\n| `tormach-lathe.cps`: write the retract as `G0` | red: `tormach_lathe_feeds_in_and_feeds_out_of_the_reamed_hole`, the dwell test, the golden test |\n| scripts restored | green: 7 of 7 |\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (100 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nThe gate and the tests ran with `RUSTC_WRAPPER` empty and a private target directory. The shared sccache server did not answer compile requests on this machine during the run.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone moved. Two goldens are new:\n\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/fanuc-lathe.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/tormach-lathe.nc`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on a control or a machine. The goldens record our mapping only.\n- The retract feed of `G85` on a Fanuc T-series control was not compared with a control manual. The post states \"feed in, feed out at F\".\n- A ream in a C-axis (live-tool) section was not posted. `fanuc-lathe.cps` refuses each drilling cycle in a C-axis section by name. That refusal has no test here.\n- `fanuc-lathe` posts the chain of a refused off-axis ream as plain `G01` moves. The program has a warning and is never released. This PR does not change that.\n- The inch unit was not posted.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1481\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
